@page board_stm32vldiscovery STM32VLDISCOVERY
@tableofcontents

<div class="hc-board-header">
<div>
The `stm32vldiscovery` target supports ST's STM32VLDISCOVERY board with an
STM32F100RB. With 8 KB of RAM it is the smallest HomeCore target. It runs the
shell and VFS over a USART1 console (interrupt-driven receive) with a 1 kHz SysTick.
<div class="hc-badges"><span class="hc-badge hc-ok">QEMU tested in CI</span><span class="hc-badge hc-pending">Hardware pending</span></div>
QEMU's `stm32vldiscovery` machine runs this port, so it is the STM32 code path
covered by the CI regression. The physical-board build, which adds PLL clock
setup, has not been validated on hardware.
</div>
<div class="hc-spec-panel">
